;; Package x86i is Arbace's x86-64 machine (doc/asm/AMD64.md §10; AX5-DESIGN, AXS51-AXS62): a Linux process's integer
;; instructions interpreted over emu's address space and kernel, decoded by LLVM's X86 disassembler rebuilt from the table
;; (decode.go over dgen's dectab.go), each mnemonic's family hand-written from the Intel SDM and the AMD APM as references
;; (sem.go), the flags computed lazily (flags.go). An instruction no family claims raises SIGILL with the class
;; :unimplemented, never a silent wrong result.
